# Secrets
# `.env` is now ignored too. It previously carried only the URL, project id and
# publishable key, but it pointed at a DIFFERENT Supabase project than the one
# we deploy against -- committing it would ship the wrong backend. Production
# configuration lives in Vercel environment variables instead; see
# DEPLOYMENT.md. `.env.example` documents the required names.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.development.local
*.key
*.pem
service-account*.json

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Leftover empty dir from the initial clone (locked by a process on Windows).
edu/

# Supabase CLI local runtime state. `.temp/` holds generated Kong / edge-runtime
# secrets for the LOCAL stack -- real key material that must never be committed.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Stray screenshot output from an e2e run invoked without a path argument.
undefined/

# Desktop app (ADR-010): built UI and Rust output
dist-desktop
# Generated per build by scripts/build-desktop.mjs (this build's backend in the CSP)
src-tauri/tauri.build.conf.json
